{
  "configuration_id": "config_030",
  "reason": "1) Evidence/uncertainty: The RNA branch is well-characterized (scvi_n200 + multiprofile + avgpool = 0.650 is the current best), but the image modality's contribution in a fused setting is completely untested. Image-only ResNet50 was very weak (0.208), yet this was under a single-profile, no-aggregation setup and with a fundamentally different encoder architecture, so it does not definitively rule out complementary image signal. 2) What this tests: config_030 pairs the best known RNA configuration (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) with the ResNet50 image branch via the simplest fusion (concat), isolating the question 'does adding the image modality to a strong RNA signal improve validation accuracy over RNA-only?' 3) Why it is the best use of budget: This is the highest-information experiment for the overall search. A positive result opens the entire multimodal design space (fusion strategy, image encoder, aggregation) and justifies further investment. A null or negative result eliminates ~30 multimodal configurations from consideration and redirects remaining budget toward RNA-encoder refinement (e.g., scgpt) or alternative image encoders (ViT-L). Testing this directional question before exploring encoder variants or fusion strategies avoids spending multiple experiments on a modality that may not contribute."
}

